            <ArticleTitle>[Cyst of the major omentum--laparoscopic diagnosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1010-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report describes the case of a 22-year-old female patient with noncharacteristic complaints in the lower abdomen. Sonography revealed a large cyst close to the right adnexa, suggestive of adnexitis; however, laparoscopy, performed because of suspected adnexitis, revealed a cystic tumor connected to the omentum instead.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
